+## Git Synchronization
+
+- `obsidian-cli create` and `obsidian-cli edit` synchronously fetch, rebase, commit, and push after a successful write.
+- If a note must be changed with a direct file-writing tool, run `/home/openclaw/.local/bin/obsidian-git-sync` immediately afterward.
+- A systemd timer also fetches, rebases, commits, and pushes every five minutes so edits from other devices reach the server.
+- Never claim that an edit is available on other devices if the Git sync command failed.
+
